    <tags>bff-api, communication, architecture</tags>
    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>Introduces a NET-NEW channel-extensibility seam (`ICommunicationChannelIngestor`) into shared `Services/Communication/` — completes ADR-045's stated-but-unbuilt inbound intent — plus the first implementation (`MessagingIngestor`). Architecture-shaping, BFF-touching (`.cs`, Services/Communication hot-path), requires publish-size + CVE + code-review + adr-check per root §10 and §11 Component Justification for the new seam.</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W2</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <fr-refs>FR-02</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Add the **net-new inbound seam** that completes ADR-045's stated-but-unbuilt intent, alongside the shipped sender/archiver seams:

    • **`ICommunicationChannelIngestor`** `[NEW seam]` — the "ingest" leg counterpart to `ICommunicationChannelSender` / `ICommunicationArchiver`. One implementation per `CommunicationType`; keyed by `SupportedType` for the same additive-registration pattern the dispatcher already uses. It accepts a channel-normalized inbound message (a `NormalizedMessage`, the envelope the engine already operates over) and persists it as a `sprk_communication` record, then hands off to the shared enrichment/association path — so inbound capture is channel-agnostic instead of forked per channel. Define the interface + its channel-neutral request/result shape mirroring `ICommunicationChannelSender`'s DTO discipline (no provider types across the seam).

    • **`MessagingIngestor`** `[NEW impl]` — implements `ICommunicationChannelIngestor` with `SupportedType =&gt; CommunicationType.Message`. It is the persist-side of the inbound ACS path: given a normalized ACS message, it creates/updates the `sprk_communication` (type=Message) record and invokes enrichment best-effort. The actual Event Grid ingress + Service Bus job + ACS-event→`NormalizedMessage` normalizer are tasks 030/031 which call INTO this seam — do NOT build them here.

    Register the seam + impl in `CommunicationModule` (ADR-010, unconditional), keyed by `CommunicationType`, resolvable via the same dispatch mechanism as the sender/archiver seams (extend `CommunicationChannelDispatcher` with a `ResolveIngestor(type)` OR add a parallel keyed resolver — mirror the existing shape). Do NOT modify the existing email `IncomingCommunicationProcessor` behavior in this task (040 later assigns threads on that path; email inbound stays green). This task defines the seam and the messaging impl only.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke BFF Communication architect. Authority on `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/`. Fluent in ADR-045 (channel seams — sender/archiver shipped; ingestor is the missing leg), ADR-046 (ACS messaging channel — task 007), ADR-010 (DI minimalism), ADR-032 (Null-Object), §11 Component Justification, and `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A net-new `ICommunicationChannelIngestor` seam exists in `Services/Communication/Channels/`, shaped as the inbound counterpart to the sender/archiver seams (channel-neutral input `NormalizedMessage`, keyed by `SupportedType`), resolvable via the dispatcher. `MessagingIngestor` (`SupportedType = Message`) implements it: persists an inbound ACS message as a `sprk_communication` (type=Message) record and invokes enrichment best-effort. Both are registered in `CommunicationModule`, unconditional. The existing email `IncomingCommunicationProcessor` is unchanged. Build clean; seam + impl tests pass; publish-size (vs ~45.30 MB) + CVE + bff-extensions Placement Justification + §11 Component Justification reported; `/conflict-check` before PR.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      **Mirror the email seam — and complete it.** email-r4 (task 016) shipped the OUTBOUND channel seams: `ICommunicationChannelSender` + `ICommunicationArchiver`, keyed by `CommunicationType` and resolved by `CommunicationChannelDispatcher` (`ToDictionary(SupportedType)`; additive registration; engine/enrichment/regarding/review UI never change to add a channel). But inbound was left CONCRETE and email-only: `IncomingCommunicationProcessor` + `Engine/` fetch Graph messages directly — there is **no ingestor seam** (design §2 "Inbound ingestor seam — NONE"). Messaging's inbound is net-new, and design §10 / §3.1 direct R1 to abstract it as a seam now, so inbound is not messaging-forked and the platform gains the missing leg of ADR-045's stated intent.

      **§11 Component Justification (the NEW seam — the one that needs justifying).**
      • Existing: NO ingestor seam exists — verified by grep (`grep -rn "ICommunicationChannelIngestor" src/` returns nothing; inbound today is the concrete `IncomingCommunicationProcessor`). The sender/archiver seams exist but are the OUTBOUND legs; there is no inbound counterpart.
      • Extension: cannot be an extension of `IncomingCommunicationProcessor` — that is a concrete, email-and-Graph-specific class, not a seam; making messaging call it would fork it with ACS branches. The seam is the boundary that keeps inbound channel-agnostic.
      • Cost-of-doing-nothing (concrete contract failure): without `ICommunicationChannelIngestor`, the inbound ACS capture pipeline (030/031) would have to persist messaging directly against a bespoke messaging-only path OR branch `IncomingCommunicationProcessor` on channel — either way inbound forks per channel, violating ADR-045's one-process principle and re-opening the engine/enrichment for the next channel (SMS in R2). The seam is what lets 030/031 call one channel-agnostic ingest boundary.

      Scope discipline: this task defines the seam + the messaging impl + their registration ONLY. The Event Grid webhook ingress + subscription-validation handshake (030), the Service Bus job + ACS-event→`NormalizedMessage` normalizer + idempotent dedupe + DLQ (031) call INTO this seam and are separate tasks. Do NOT modify email inbound behavior (040 handles the shared-path thread-assignment edit under characterization tests).
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Channels/ICommunicationChannelSender.cs</file>
