  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-02">Add the `ICommunicationChannelIngestor` seam; `MessagingIngestor` persists an inbound normalized ACS message as `sprk_communication` and hands off to enrichment. (Event Grid ingress + job + normalizer + idempotency are 030/031, which call this seam.)</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-045">The ingestor is the missing inbound leg of the channel seams — keyed by `CommunicationType`, additive registration, resolved via the dispatcher. The engine, enrichment, regarding model, and review UI MUST NOT change to add an inbound channel (NFR-04). Operate over the `NormalizedMessage` envelope only — never `Azure.Communication.*` or `Microsoft.Graph.Message` across the seam.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-046">Follow ADR-046 (task 007): ACS is transport, Dataverse is the record; the ingestor seam is codified there as a reusable addition.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">Register the seam + `MessagingIngestor` via `CommunicationModule` only, keyed to `CommunicationType.Message`, unconditional (ADR-032 Null-Object if any dependency is feature-gated).</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-02">Enrichment/association invoked by the ingestor MUST be best-effort and non-fatal — enrichment failure MUST NOT fail the persist. Persist every message as `sprk_communication` (Dataverse is the record).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Do NOT modify the existing email `IncomingCommunicationProcessor` behavior in this task — email inbound stays green (thread-assignment edit is 040 under characterization tests). Do NOT build the Event Grid ingress/job/normalizer/idempotency (030/031).</constraint>
    <constraint source="root §10">bff-extensions Placement Justification in the PR (ingestor lives in BFF — sole `sprk_communication` mutation + policy point); publish-size delta vs ~45.30 MB baseline; no new HIGH CVE. Run `/conflict-check` before PR (shared `Services/Communication/` hot-path).</constraint>
    <constraint source="§11">State the concrete cost-of-doing-nothing for the new seam (inbound forks per channel; engine/enrichment re-opened for SMS in R2) in the PR — a NEW seam requires a §11 justification with grep evidence that no ingestor seam exists.</constraint>
  </constraints>

