    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Channel seam interface shape" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Channels/ICommunicationChannelSender.cs">
        `SupportedType` dispatch key + a channel-neutral request record (no provider types). `ICommunicationChannelIngestor` mirrors this: `SupportedType` + a channel-neutral input built around `NormalizedMessage`.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Type-keyed dispatch resolution" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Channels/CommunicationChannelDispatcher.cs">
        `IEnumerable&lt;T&gt;` ctor injection + `ToDictionary(x =&gt; x.SupportedType)` + `Resolve*(type)` throwing `CHANNEL_NOT_SUPPORTED`. Add `ResolveIngestor(type)` (or a parallel resolver) the same way.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Envelope-only engine boundary" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Models/NormalizedMessage.cs">
        The Association Engine + enrichment operate over `NormalizedMessage` only. The ingestor accepts this type; the ACS→envelope mapping happens at the pipeline boundary in 031's normalizer, not inside the ingestor.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps>
    <step order="1">Read `ICommunicationChannelSender.cs` + `ICommunicationArchiver.cs` + `CommunicationChannelDispatcher.cs` to fix the seam + dispatch shape to mirror. Read `NormalizedMessage.cs` (the envelope the ingestor accepts) and `IncomingCommunicationProcessor.cs` + `CommunicationEnrichmentService.cs` to see how email currently persists + enriches (so the seam abstracts the same downstream handoff).</step>
    <step order="2">Grep-confirm no `ICommunicationChannelIngestor` exists today (§11 evidence). Read `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` §F + §11 + the ADR-046 ingestor-seam section (task 007).</step>
    <step order="3">Define `ICommunicationChannelIngestor` in `Services/Communication/Channels/`: `CommunicationType SupportedType { get; }` + `Task&lt;...&gt; IngestAsync(&lt;channel-neutral input around NormalizedMessage&gt;, CancellationToken)`. Define its channel-neutral request/result records mirroring `ChannelSendRequest`/`ChannelSendResult` discipline (no provider types).</step>
    <step order="4">Implement `MessagingIngestor : ICommunicationChannelIngestor` (`SupportedType =&gt; CommunicationType.Message`): persist the normalized inbound ACS message as a `sprk_communication` (Direction=Incoming, type=Message) record via the canonical Dataverse service, then invoke enrichment best-effort (NFR-02). Reuse the same persist/enrich downstream email uses; do NOT re-fetch from ACS here (031's normalizer supplies the `NormalizedMessage`).</step>
    <step order="5">Wire dispatch: extend `CommunicationChannelDispatcher` with `ResolveIngestor(CommunicationType)` (or a parallel keyed resolver) using the same `IEnumerable` + `ToDictionary(SupportedType)` pattern. Register the seam + `MessagingIngestor` in `CommunicationModule` (ADR-010, unconditional).</step>
    <step order="6">Grep-verify the existing email `IncomingCommunicationProcessor`, the engine, enrichment, regarding model, and review UI are UNCHANGED by this task (the ingestor is additive; email inbound is untouched until 040).</step>
    <step order="7">Write tests: `ResolveIngestor(Message)` returns `MessagingIngestor`; `IngestAsync` persists exactly one `sprk_communication` (type=Message) from a `NormalizedMessage` and invokes enrichment; enrichment failure does NOT fail the persist (NFR-02); `ResolveIngestor(Email)` (no email ingestor registered in R1) throws `CHANNEL_NOT_SUPPORTED` as designed. Prefer vertical-slice seam tests per ADR-038.</step>
    <step order="8">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` + `dotnet test tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ --filter Communication`; confirm existing email inbound tests still pass (unchanged behavior).</step>
    <step order="9.1">Run `dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o c:/tmp/msg-021-publish/`; report compressed size + delta vs ~45.30 MB baseline. Expected ≈ 0 (pure code, no new package). ≥+5 MB justify; ≥55 MB architecture review; ≥60 MB HARD STOP.</step>
    <step order="9.2">Run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` — confirm no new HIGH-severity CVE.</step>
    <step order="9.5">FULL-rigor quality gates: `code-review` on the diff; `adr-check` against `spec.md` (focus ADR-045 seam completion + §11 new-seam justification + ADR-010/032 DI + NFR-02 non-fatal enrichment). Resolve Critical findings (path C) or surface an ADR conflict (root §6.5).</step>
    <step order="10">Run `/conflict-check` before the PR (shared `Services/Communication/` BFF hot-path).</step>
    <step order="11">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (021 ✅) + `current-task.md`; record decisions (ingestor seam signature, dispatch mechanism `ResolveIngestor` vs parallel resolver, the ingest input shape 030/031 must produce).</step>
  </steps>

