  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">`ICommunicationChannelIngestor` exists in `Services/Communication/Channels/` with a `SupportedType` dispatch key and a channel-neutral `IngestAsync` operating over `NormalizedMessage` (no `Azure.Communication.*` / `Microsoft.Graph` type in the signature).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`MessagingIngestor : ICommunicationChannelIngestor` exists with `SupportedType =&gt; CommunicationType.Message`; `IngestAsync` persists exactly one `sprk_communication` (Direction=Incoming, type=Message) from a `NormalizedMessage`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Enrichment/association invoked by the ingestor is best-effort — a thrown enrichment error does NOT fail the persist (NFR-02).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The dispatcher resolves the ingestor by `CommunicationType` (`ResolveIngestor(Message)` → `MessagingIngestor`); the seam + impl are registered via `CommunicationModule`, unconditional.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The existing email `IncomingCommunicationProcessor`, the engine, enrichment, regarding model, and review UI are byte-unchanged by this task (grep/diff-verifiable).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No Event Grid ingress / Service Bus job / normalizer / idempotency logic is added here (those are 030/031) — this task is seam + impl + registration only.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`dotnet build` clean; existing email inbound tests pass; publish-size delta ≈ 0 vs ~45.30 MB; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Depends only on 007 (ADR-046 codifies the ingestor seam). Blocks 030 (Event Grid ingress → job) and 031 (normalizer → `NormalizedMessage` → this ingestor's `IngestAsync` with idempotent dedupe). `parallel-safe: true` within W2 — distinct new files from 020 (sender/archiver); both touch `CommunicationModule` (coordinate the two small registration edits at merge, or serialize the module edit).

    Strict scope: define the seam + messaging impl + registration. The idempotency/echo-dedup, DLQ, Event Grid handshake, and Service Bus job are 030/031 and call INTO `IngestAsync`. If the seam seems to need Event Grid or ACS-fetch knowledge, it is mis-shaped — the ingestor accepts an already-normalized `NormalizedMessage` and knows nothing about transport (that boundary is 031's normalizer). Do NOT touch email inbound (040 owns the shared-path thread edit under characterization tests).
  </notes>

